lines = []
for i, (d, p) in enumerate(cands, 3):
    refs.append({"path": str(p), "role": f"candidate, claimed direction {d}"}); lines.append(f"Image {i} claims {d}. EXPECTED for {d}: {T[d]}")
text = (f"JUDGE BURST {bid} — the Necromancer's turnaround, OWNER-CHECKLIST pass (Run C-6 P2): every item below was a defect the owner found in the previous pass; verify each by looking, not by claim. task_id \"{bid}\". You are a separate instance: you have not seen any prompt, receipt, check or prior judgment, and must not look for one.\n\n"
 "Image 1 is the owner's master at full resolution — read the INVARIANTS from it: PALE ICE-BLUE eyes; a ROUND PLAIN SILVER belt disc with a small leaf-like sigil (NO skull); a POLISHED SILVER-STEEL ribcage relief on a black cuirass (metal, not bone); ONE bone horn on HIS LEFT shoulder, nothing on the right; a small dark-leather TOME at his LEFT hip with SILVER CORNER CAPS and a short RED RIBBON marker, no other emblem; a war scythe in EXACTLY TWO gauntleted hands, HELD OUT IN FRONT of him (haft away from the chest, upper hand extended at shoulder height); NO skull anywhere on him. Image 2 is the same master at the scene camera: an elevated view looking DOWN ~53° (crown and shoulder tops seen from above, feet foreshortened) at cell scale — the camera and scale every candidate must match.\n"
 "GEOMETRY RULE (sides) — key MIRRORING on the HORN and the TOME, which are fixed to his LEFT side: turned toward screen-RIGHT he shows his RIGHT side (horn and tome FAR, behind); toward screen-LEFT his LEFT side (horn on the NEAR shoulder, tome on the NEAR hip); back views: horn SCREEN-LEFT of the head. The SCYTHE is hand-held and, in this set, HELD OUT IN FRONT with the blade hooking FORWARD — so the blade may sit ahead of the body in ANY facing; its position alone never makes a candidate mirrored. Horn/tome on the wrong side for the claim = MIRRORED. Judge each candidate independently; do not assume any is a control or correct.\n\n"
 + "\n".join(lines) +
 "\n\nFor EACH candidate write the CHECKLIST as booleans, each with one line of visible evidence:\n"
 "eyes_blue (pale blue irises visible; if the face is hidden write null) · head_level (HARD: the face is NOT angled toward the ground at all — chin level or fractionally raised, eyes on the horizon; any downward bow = false; if the face is hidden judge from the skull/hair angle) · head_aligned (not tilted sideways, not turned against the body) · no_skull_buckle · no_skull_shoulder · no_skull_book · ribcage_steel (silver metal, not bone/ivory; null if the back is shown) · tome_master_ornament (corner caps + red ribbon, nothing else; null if hidden) · hands_exactly_two (exactly two gauntlets, both on the haft, none emerging from the torso or floating) · hands_in_front (back views: no arms bent behind the back; null for front views) · right_hand_upper (HARD: the RIGHT hand is the upper grip near the blade head, the LEFT the lower grip — arms swapped = false) · upper_arm_bent (HARD: the upper arm is bent at the elbow, forearm roughly level; a locked-straight or raised-high arm = false) · haft_straight (one straight shaft with wrapped grips and a butt spike; a bent, kinked or detail-less haft = false) · haft_forward45 (the haft angles forward about 45° clear of the chest, blade head ahead at about head height; resting on the chest/shoulder or near-vertical = false) · blade_forward (HARD: the crescent hooks FORWARD — its curve and tip point in the direction he faces: screen-left for W/SW/NW, screen-right for E/SE/NE, toward the viewer's left for S as in Image 1, away for N; a blade hooking behind him = false) · haft_diagonal (HARD: the haft runs on a diagonal held out in front — low hand near the far hip, upper hand extended at shoulder height; a vertical haft held like a standard or flag = false) · scythe_held_out (HARD: the scythe is HELD OUT IN FRONT as in Image 1 — the haft stands away from the chest, the upper hand extended forward/outward at about shoulder height; a haft resting against the torso or hugged to the chest = false) · buckle_detail (the round silver belt disc with its small sigil is clearly drawn; a blank or smeared disc = false; null if hidden) · standing_upright (HARD: an at-ease STANDING rest — legs straight, feet under the hips, torso upright, no crouch, no wide fighting stance, no forward lean) · camera_matches (crown/shoulder tops seen from above and feet foreshortened as in Image 2 — not eye-level, not shallower) · scale_matches (sole-to-crown height the same fraction of the canvas as Image 2, ±10 %) · mirrored (sides swapped for the claim) · seen_facing.\n"
 "Then axes 1–5 (integers, one-line reasons): 1 register · 2 identity (count the checklist falses) · 3 light (key screen upper-left) · 4 equipment geometry vs EXPECTED (all correct = 5; each error −1; mirrored = 1) · 5 direction read at 64 px.\n"
 "Write out/judgment.json: {\"candidates\":[{\"image\":n,\"claimed\":\"…\",\"seen_facing\":\"…\",\"checklist\":{\"eyes_blue\":bool|null,\"head_level\":bool,\"head_aligned\":bool,\"no_skull_buckle\":bool,\"no_skull_shoulder\":bool,\"no_skull_book\":bool,\"ribcage_steel\":bool|null,\"tome_master_ornament\":bool|null,\"hands_exactly_two\":bool,\"hands_in_front\":bool|null,\"right_hand_upper\":bool,\"upper_arm_bent\":bool,\"haft_straight\":bool,\"haft_forward45\":bool,\"blade_forward\":bool,\"haft_diagonal\":bool,\"scythe_held_out\":bool,\"buckle_detail\":bool|null,\"standing_upright\":bool,\"camera_matches\":bool,\"scale_matches\":bool},\"evidence\":{\"head_level\":\"…\",…},\"mirrored\":bool,\"axes\":{\"1\":n,…},\"reasons\":{\"4\":\"…\",…}}, …]}. No image_gen. No code. No web. No files outside out/. calls_used must be 0.\n"
 f"RETURN: receipt task_id \"{bid}\"; images []; files [out/judgment.json + sha256]; status DELIVERED / DELIVERED_WITH_CONCERNS; concerns for anything you could not assess. Never PASS/FAIL — booleans and scores only.")
task = {"text": text, "references": refs, "image_cap": 0, "minutes_cap": 15, "tool_call_cap": 20, "outputs": ["out/judgment.json"], "effort": "high", "add_dirs": [], "experiment": "C6-P2"}
json.dump(task, open(B/f'briefs/C-6/{bid}.task.json', 'w'), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)
print(bid, 'control = mirror of', ctrl_src, 'claimed', ctrl_claim, 'at image', [i for i,(d,p) in enumerate(cands,3) if p==cp][0], '| chars', len(text))
